 - **[Screen Model] vt100 0.16.2 as a pre-send readiness gate only.** After `turn-ended`, the gate waits for the screen to go quiet, then requires the absence of every known modal signature and waits, up to its maximum wait, for the version-stamped input-box signature. As landed, the model is the pure `viola_agent_claude::screen::Screen` (no I/O, no clock read; every instant is a parameter), and `run` feeds it on its own feed thread (`src/run/gate.rs`): a tee on the pump output writes the human's bytes first and then offers a copy with `try_send` into a queue bounded at `FEED_CAPACITY` = 256 messages (`sync_channel`; the pump copies at most 8192 bytes per write, so at most 2 MiB waits for the model), so the passthrough never waits on the model. The `Screen` sits behind a mutex shared by the feed thread and the `Gate` handle `send` reads (`Gate::wait_ready`, re-read every 20 ms); each feed and resize runs under `catch_unwind` inside that lock. A caught vt100 panic poisons the model until the host size changes, and so does a message the full queue drops (a dropped byte desynchronises the screen): one `parse-rejected{parser:"vt100-feed", detail:"oversize"}` per poisoning episode, and a size message carries the drop count at its offer, so a drop after a queued resize poisons the fresh screen again. A poisoned model reads `input-not-ready`. The quiet period (`QUIET_PERIOD` = 300 ms) and the maximum wait (`GATE_MAX_WAIT` = 8.5 s) are compiled built-ins in `viola-agent-claude`, validated per CLI version by the stamped `quiet-period` row (the ready and turn screens settle within `GATE_MAX_WAIT`). The maximum wait was 5 s until chunk 2026-10-07-send-waits-out-the-paste-hint raised it on the founder's live ruling of 2026-10-07T10:29Z (relayed by the overseer), so that it covers the CLI's 8.0 s paste hint ([CLI Version Compatibility]); the quiet period is unchanged. As measured on 2.1.287 at that chunk (`evidence/reverify-round.md`), the ready screen settled in 1 103 ms and the turn screen in 617 ms. The signatures are compiled in `viola_agent_claude::screen::SIGNATURES`: `input_box: ["for agents"]` and `modals: ["Yes, I trust this folder", "Yes, allow external imports"]` (`Signatures::holds_any`). A screen is ready when a row contains an input-box literal and no row contains a modal literal. The per-version `modal-signature` row (an untrusted start shows a compiled modal literal) and `input-box-signature` row (the ready and turn screens hold the input-box literal and no modal) validate them. They landed with chunk 2026-10-05-real-cli-verify-probes, through the typed-input `viola verify` probe the founder ratified live on 2026-10-05 (relayed by the overseer), which runs the installed `claude` locally on the dev host only. `run` passes `Some(&SIGNATURES)` to `gate::start` exactly when its version gate read `cli_verified` (`Launched.cli_verified`): the full gate on a verified CLI version, and the partial gate otherwise. The verdict's consumer is confirmed `send`. On a verified CLI a modal row refuses at once, and a quiet screen with no input-box row keeps the gate waiting for one until `GATE_MAX_WAIT` has passed since the send entered the gate. A screen not quiet within the maximum wait, a poisoned model and a quiet screen still without an input-box row at the bound are refused: `send` types nothing and reports `not-delivered` with detail `input-not-ready`. The wait lives in the pure verdict (`Screen::verdict` reads `waiting_since`), so `Gate::wait_ready` did not change for it. Rationale: CLI-native modals bypass every hook (measured on 2.1.280: the "Teach auto mode…" modal swallowed a paste), and the screen lags the hooks. Signatures are compiled literals that each version's stamp validates. On a CLI version with no passing stamp the gate is partial: `Screen::verdict(None, …)` still refuses a poisoned model and a screen not quiet within the maximum wait, and a quiet screen is ready with no row read, so delivery confirmation decides the re