-- **[Delivery Confirmation] Every `send` is confirmed.** If no matching `prompt-submitted` arrives within the confirmation window, the send is reported as `not-delivered` with detail `no-prompt-submitted`. The confirmation window is the compiled `CONFIRM_WINDOW_FALLBACK` = 10 s in `viola_agent_claude::screen`, never in `config.json`. It is no longer provisional: the per-version `confirm-window` ledger row validates it (the typed prompt reaches UserPromptSubmit within the window, measured as `measured.typed_probe.prompt_latency_ms`), and `run` reads no window number from the stamp. `send` blocks for at most the readiness gate's maximum wait, plus the atomic paste, plus the window (18.5 s with the compiled 8.5 s and 10 s), and returns its result no later than when the window closes. On the MCP surface that total must stay below the MCP client's tool-call timeout. Matching compares the typed text (the sent text with every CR LF pair and every other CR as one LF, and without its trailing CR and LF characters, below) with `prompt-submitted`'s `text` exactly (nothing else is trimmed), whatever `origin` the hook filed, `harness` included, after `viola-agent-claude` has normalised it: first the `<pasted_content id=…>` wrapper the CLI puts around long pastes is removed together with the frame the CLI writes around it (the two newlines directly before the open tag, the one directly after the close tag, and a second after it when text follows that is not the next pair's own frame), then the CLI's escaping of tag-like text is reversed (the landed `long-paste-wrapper` and `tag-escaping` rows). The wrapper-side matcher therefore never sees a Claude-specific shape, and a literal `<\pasted_content` the user typed is never mistaken for the wrapper. `send` types a text with every CR LF pair and every other CR inside it as one LF, and without its trailing CR and LF characters (trailing LF: the founder's ruling, live, 2026-10-07T15:21Z, relayed by the overseer, landed at chunk 2026-10